        "id": "p44-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Let $x$ be the number of people who travelled overseas and interstate only.\n\nLet $y$ be the number of people who travelled overseas only.\n\nSolve simultaneously to find $x$ and $y$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=4$, $y=2$.",
          "worked": "Using the total of 38 people,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n22+7+x+y+3&=38\\\\\nx+y&=6\\hspace{8mm}\\text{(1)}\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe overseas total equals the own-state-only count:\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny+x+2+2&=18-2x\\\\\n3x+y&=14\\qquad\\text{(2)}\n\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (1) from (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}\n2x&=8\\\\\nx&=4\\\\\ny&=6-4\\\\\ny&=2.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q8-c",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "If one person from the 38 is chosen at random, find the probability that they have travelled:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p44-q8-c-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "Within their own state only",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{5}{19}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Own state only}&=18-2(4)=10\\\\\nP(\\text{own state only})&=\\frac{10}{38}=\\frac{5}{19}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 14
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q8-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "Overseas only",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{19}$",
              "worked": "$$P(\\text{overseas only})=\\frac{y}{38}=\\frac{2}{38}=\\frac{1}{19}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q8-c-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "Interstate only",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{7}{38}$",
              "worked": "$$P(\\text{interstate only})=\\frac{7}{38}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q8-c-iv",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iv",
            "prompt": "Overseas or interstate or within their own state",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{35}{38}$",
              "worked": "Three people did not travel at all.\n$$P(O\\cup I\\cup S)=\\frac{38-3}{38}=\\frac{35}{38}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 14
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q8-c-v",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "v",
            "prompt": "Interstate or overseas",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{25}{38}$",
              "worked": "Exclude the 10 people who travelled within their own state only and the 3 who did not travel.\n$$P(I\\cup O)=\\frac{38-10-3}{38}=\\frac{25}{38}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 14
          }
